From 2274dcfb1eeae5a96d7d1f2264f4a6541ee2af4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:39:06 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(api): add 15-second timeout to client-side fetch
 requests
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The shared request() function in src/lib/api.ts called fetch()
with no timeout — a stalled server response left the user staring
at a spinner indefinitely. Add AbortSignal.timeout(15_000) so
after 15 seconds the fetch aborts and React Query shows the
existing retryable error state (ErrorState with a "retry" button).

Matches the 15-second timeout the server's ESPN client already
uses (server/espn/client.ts line 29). No other files change —
the timeout is a one-line addition to the shared request path.

